course: dictionary
lesson: 12009
title: Cheerfulness and feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cheerfulness means being happy, bright and in a good mood, and showing it to other people. You can see it in a smile, a warm voice or a friendly wave.
explain: «Her cheerfulness made the whole class smile.» Cheerfulness is a noun, a thing you can have. The describing word is cheerful: «She is cheerful.» Adding -ness turns the describing word into a thing.
explain: Cheerfulness is something you share. A person can feel happy inside, but cheerfulness is the bright mood they show to others. «Mum greeted us with her usual cheerfulness.» The word usual tells you she is cheerful most days.
explain: Teachers and stories often praise cheerfulness. «The team played with cheerfulness, even when they were losing.» Cheerfulness also helps people get through hard times. To check a meaning, swap in happy and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Cheerfulness is a noun, so you can have it, show it or be praised for it.
fact: «Cheerful» is the describing word, and «cheerfulness» is the noun made from it.
fact: Cheerfulness means being happy, bright and in a good mood, and showing it to others.
fact: «With cheerfulness» means happily and brightly, as in «She sang with cheerfulness.»
fact: People often use cheerfulness to get through hard times, such as being ill or having a bad day.
exercise: «Her cheerfulness made the whole class smile.» What does cheerfulness mean here? | Being angry with the class | *Being happy and bright, and sharing a good mood | Being tired after a long day | Being quiet and still
exercise: «The team played with cheerfulness, even when they were losing.» Which word is closest in meaning to cheerfulness? | Anger | Silence | *Happiness | Sadness
exercise: Which word is the noun made from cheerful, a thing you can have? | sadly | cheerful | cheerless | *cheerfulness
test: «Mum greeted us with her usual cheerfulness.» What does the word usual tell you? | *Mum is cheerful most days | Mum is cheerful only today | Mum is angry at us | Mum is never cheerful
test: «He showed cheerfulness when he lost the match.» Which is a good way to show cheerfulness? | Hiding in your room | Frowning and folding your arms | Shouting at the referee | *Smiling and saying well played to everyone
exam: Which word means being bright and in a good mood, and showing it to others? | *Cheerfulness | Boredom | Tiredness | Gloominess
